# Trivy ignore rules for Twinbox
# See: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore

# CVE-2026-33671: picomatch Regular Expression Denial of Service
# Location: npm transitive dependency (node_modules/picomatch)
# Status: Fixed in picomatch 4.0.4, but npm 11.x bundles 4.0.3 internally.
# Risk: LOW for our use case — picomatch is used only at build time / dev tooling.
# Action: Will be resolved automatically when npm updates its bundled version.
CVE-2026-33671

# CVE-2026-34986: go-jose/v4 vulnerability
# Location: /usr/local/bin/tofu, /usr/local/bin/helm, /usr/local/bin/kubectl
# Status: Fixed in go-jose 4.1.4, awaiting upstream releases.
# Risk: MEDIUM — these are CLI tools, not long-running services.
# Action: Will be resolved when OpenTofu, Helm, and kubectl release new builds.
CVE-2026-34986

# CVE-2026-33186: google.golang.org/grpc CRITICAL vulnerability
# Location: /usr/local/bin/tofu, /usr/local/bin/helm, /usr/local/bin/kubectl
# Status: Fixed in grpc-go 1.79.3, awaiting upstream releases.
# Risk: MEDIUM — these are CLI tools, not long-running services.
# Action: Will be resolved when OpenTofu, Helm, and kubectl release new builds.
CVE-2026-33186
